You have used `Future`, `Poll`, `Context`, `Waker` and `pin!` without the full story. Here it is. The standard library defines:

```rust
pub trait Future {
    type Output;
    fn poll(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Self::Output>;
}

pub enum Poll<T> {
    Ready(T),
    Pending,
}
```

- `Output` is what the future produces: for `async fn f() -> u32`, it is `u32`.
- `poll` tries to make progress. It returns `Ready(value)` when done, or `Pending` if it must wait.
- The **contract**: a future that returns `Pending` must make sure `cx.waker()` is woken when it can make progress. Otherwise nobody will poll it again and it hangs.
- After `Ready`, a future must not be polled again.

